{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456955-how-do-you-handle-primium-from-a-game-mechanics-standpoint","id":1456955,"title":"How do you handle Primium from a game mechanics standpoint?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-16T05:28:55-07:00","id":1456955,"title":"How do you handle Primium from a game mechanics standpoint?","content":"At our table there is a discussion of how to handle Primium. Can you just aim a spell near the protected character to sidestep the Primium? Specifically here is how we have been handling different cases for my character who has 3 points of Primium. If you could comment whether each sounds reasonable, or if you do it differently, that would be really helpful.<br /> <br /> 1) Perception effects (all 1-dot sphere effects) are unaffected by Primium.<br /> 2) Direct spells ARE resisted (i.e. Correspondence 3 teleporting, Entropy 4 direct damage, most Life and Mind effects, direct Prime and Time effects).<br /> 3) Indirect spells are NOT resisted (i.e. Forces 3 &amp; Prime 3 attacks, Correspondence 4 portals)<br /> <br /> In short, how do you handle the game mechanics of Primium at your table?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T05:57:57-07:00","id":1456958,"title":"","content":"Perception effects against primium is like Superman's X-ray vision versus lead. That is, primium acts as a screen that keeps you from looking inside. It's mere presence does not disrupt perception of things around it, but attempting to perceive things inside it have to overcome it's counter magic.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I tend to agree with you \u2014 though I don't judge it based off of which fear requirements are involved so much it's healthy effect is described. Primium provides no defense to dropping a safe on the target, or shooting it; but it does protect against magic that tries to trigger and internal disruption. Basically, if the magic generates an effect outside of the primium and then lets the normal \u201cphysics\u201d of the situation run its course, primium has no effect. But if the magic attempts to penetrate the primium and cause an effect on or inside it, that's when the counter magic kicks in.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, since the defining element is whether the Magick goes through the primium, Correspondence Magick can potentially bypass it \u2014 with the usual requirements of needing an appropriate connection in order to do so. If the primium is weak enough, it's often easier just to plow through it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-16-2021, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T17:43:57-07:00","id":1457929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456955-how-do-you-handle-primium-from-a-game-mechanics-standpoint#post1456955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Perception effects (all 1-dot sphere effects) are unaffected by Primium.<br /> 2) Direct spells ARE resisted (i.e. Correspondence 3 teleporting, Entropy 4 direct damage, most Life and Mind effects, direct Prime and Time effects).<br /> 3) Indirect spells are NOT resisted (i.e. Forces 3 &amp; Prime 3 attacks, Correspondence 4 portals)</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by the rules first, that's more or less how it works, except it would still stop Perception effects.<br /> <br /> Every spell is affecting or creating a Pattern, so keep this in mind. Primium basically protects a Pattern from tampering. It isn't only the Primium itself that is protected, although the Technocracy wouldn't necessarily know how to explain this, but it is fair to simplify it as Primium always protecting the object or character that includes it. You can tweak the details on any specific case because in the end, no matter how much &quot;SCIENCE!&quot; it contains, each application is a separate spell.<br /> <br /> The fine details depend a lot more on what is happening at the table. One thing to keep in mind is that Primium affects any spell, even if the caster don't think it is a spell, but a tried and true scientific achievement from the Union labs. This usually balance the thing naturally since you have to manage pros and cons. If things get out of hand the ST may consider that the mere proximity affects your Procedures, and that's it.<br /> <br /> On the Perception effects: as a rule of thumb they don't affect the Mage's Pattern to make them able to perceive things, they affect the Pattern they're going to analyze. There is a work-around, though: With Life 2 and Forces 1 a Mage can alter their own eyes to get things like night vision. The catch is that they're perceiving the secondary Patterns you emit (light, sound, etc.) instead of your Pattern directly, so they ignore your Primium, but also can't make a complete analysis of your Pattern. So they can try to x-ray you for concealed weapons, for example, but can't use Matter 1 to determine for sure if you have any and what they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T06:42:16-08:00","id":1475314,"title":"","content":"Sorry this is a bit of a necro, but rather than start another post, I still would love a bit of clarification.<br /> <br /> Specifically against Forces (and maybe Prime) magick. Would primium protect against a lightning bolt created by a Hermetic? Against a kinetic blast from a technocratic pulse rifle? What about a Prime 3 attack of concentrated primal energy?<br /> <br /> I assume the answer is no, but then I question whether Primium is worth anywhere near the points it costs as part of the Enhancements background. If it doesn't protect against the majority of ways other mages typically inflict damage, then it's really just to add extra defense against Life magick, and I guess Mind magick too. It seems.... not worth the trouble.<br /> <br /> To put it in perspective, the campaign where I played an ItX scientist with Enhancements (including primium) is now over. In all that play time, I never once got to even roll primium when it would have benefited my character. The only times I ever rolled it was when another PC was trying to teleport me somewhere, so it was only ever an annoyance against beneficial effects.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> By the same logic, can a Forces spell even be countered with countermagick? The defending mage with Forces of his own should be able to, but on the other hand the Forces pattern being created by the aggressor is being created elsewhere and then released/directed at the target. The target would have to counter a spell that is taking place some distance away and which he may not even be aware of. A lightning bolt, even if it was created by Forces magick, it is just a normal lightning bolt. Countermagick cannot be used against normal lightning bolts.<br /> <br /> It makes Forces the end-all be-all of killing other mages - it inflicts massive damage that they cannot counter and even if it could be soaked, it's pretty trivial for a mage to inflict 20+ damage with a single Forces attack and that is far too much for most splats to soak, especially a mage.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26904,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","user":"breggie","date":". 02-23-2022, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T09:12:56-08:00","id":1475325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456955-how-do-you-handle-primium-from-a-game-mechanics-standpoint?p=1475314#post1475314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically against Forces (and maybe Prime) magick. Would primium protect against a lightning bolt created by a Hermetic? Against a kinetic blast from a technocratic pulse rifle? What about a Prime 3 attack of concentrated primal energy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Primium works like standard countermagick (and also, it <i>adds </i>to it if I'm not remembering wrong), which unlike Night Folk Counterspels doesn't exclude direct damage effects.<br /> <br /> SO.<br /> <br /> I would say yes for almost all of these, especially the 3rd example but I would think the rest too.<br /> <br /> *Prime energy it's a straigthfoward construct of pure magick and I can't see how it wouldn't be suceptible to the material made to resist it (I mean, what are &quot;the normal physics of the situation&quot; for such a thing?. Why should it fly towards a target and cause damage, and not just disolve into the ether, if not by magick?).<br /> <br /> *It's unlikely for ligthinging bolts <i>to conviniently</i> fall on your enemies, if you don't alter reality a bit (directing it with your command of magick, altering the polarity of the target, etc).<br /> <br /> *The rifle could be enginereed in such a way that it doesn't count for Countermagick, but I would have to see the justification.<br /> <br /> If the mage it's using magick to <i>direct </i>energy against a <i>target</i> I would say it definitely counts for standard Countermagick (thus Primium).<br /> <br /> Otherwise: Dodge!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-23-2022, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T17:49:50-08:00","id":1475692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456955-how-do-you-handle-primium-from-a-game-mechanics-standpoint?p=1475314#post1475314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To put it in perspective, the campaign where I played an ItX scientist with Enhancements (including primium) is now over. In all that play time, I never once got to even roll primium when it would have benefited my character. The only times I ever rolled it was when another PC was trying to teleport me somewhere, so it was only ever an annoyance against beneficial effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me more that your ST was strongly biased against Primium than anything else. They should have just forbidden it if not accepting that you had it.<br /> <br /> All your examples should be affected by Primimum. The caster is creating a Magical effect and targeting you to shoot it. It should definitely work as none of those effects was in any way indirect.<br /> <br /> What would be indirect would be, lets say, use Time or Entropy to guarantee that a gas tube explodes on your face, and even then only if the explosion itself isn't enhanced, in which case the enhancement would be counteracted, and if the effect didn't targeted <i>your</i> destiny, otherwise it would be countered at the casting.<br /> <br /> Basically, there certainly are ways around Primium, it isn't the definite, ultimate protection, but the point of a work-around is that it isn't the default you should expect. Even Technocrats are rarely personally enhanced with Primium, so the idea that every single effect you ever faced in the game wouldn't be countered seems extremely fishy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}